{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4a1b2c3d-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "MentorBooking — Local",
    "description": "Tests against the local dev server (http://localhost:3000).\n\nStartup:\n  npm run local:up\n  npm run local:setup\n  npm run local:dev\n\nHappy-path order:\n  1. Students  → Create Student\n  2. Mentors   → List Mentors  (seeds mentorId; requires a mentor in DB — see note below)\n  3. Time Slots → Create Time Slot\n  4. Bookings  → Create Booking\n  5. Bookings  → Cancel Booking\n\nSeeding a mentor locally:\n  Mentors are normally imported via CSV (POST /import/mentors), which needs S3.\n  For local testing, insert one directly into DynamoDB Local:\n\n  aws dynamodb put-item \\\n    --endpoint-url http://localhost:8000 \\\n    --table-name mentors \\\n    --region us-east-1 \\\n    --item '{\n      \"mentorId\": {\"S\": \"mentor-1\"},\n      \"name\":     {\"S\": \"Bob Jones\"},\n      \"email\":    {\"S\": \"bob@example.com\"},\n      \"skills\":   {\"L\": [{\"S\": \"aws\"}, {\"S\": \"typescript\"}]},\n      \"experience\":{\"N\": \"5\"},\n      \"active\":   {\"BOOL\": true}\n    }'\n\n  Or open the DynamoDB Local shell at http://localhost:8000/shell",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "studentId", "value": "student-1", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "mentorId", "value": "mentor-1", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "slotId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "slotStart", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "slotEnd", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "bookingId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Students",
      "item": [
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000001-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
          "name": "Create Student",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('student in response', () => pm.expect(res.student).to.be.an('object'));",
                  "if (res.student) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('studentId', res.student.studentId);",
                  "    console.log('studentId saved:', res.student.studentId);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"studentId\": \"student-1\",\n  \"name\": \"Alice Smith\",\n  \"email\": \"alice@example.com\",\n  \"phone\": \"+1-555-0100\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/students",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["students"]
            },
            "description": "Register a new student. The test script saves studentId to the collection variable."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Mentors",
      "description": "Mentors must exist in the DB before these requests work.\nSee collection description for how to seed one via DynamoDB Local.",
      "item": [
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000002-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
          "name": "List Mentors",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('mentors array', () => pm.expect(res.mentors).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "if (res.mentors && res.mentors.length > 0) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('mentorId', res.mentors[0].mentorId);",
                  "    console.log('mentorId saved:', res.mentors[0].mentorId);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mentors",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mentors"]
            },
            "description": "List all active mentors. Saves the first mentorId to the collection variable."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000002-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
          "name": "List Mentors — filtered",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mentors?skill=aws&minExperience=2",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mentors"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "skill", "value": "aws", "description": "Filter by skill tag" },
                { "key": "minExperience", "value": "2", "description": "Minimum years of experience" }
              ]
            },
            "description": "List mentors filtered by skill and/or minimum experience."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Time Slots",
      "item": [
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
          "name": "Create Time Slot",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Set a slot for tomorrow 10:00 – 11:00 (local time, ISO string)",
                  "const d = new Date();",
                  "d.setDate(d.getDate() + 1);",
                  "d.setHours(10, 0, 0, 0);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('slotStart', d.toISOString());",
                  "const end = new Date(d.getTime() + 3600000);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('slotEnd', end.toISOString());"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('timeslots array', () => pm.expect(res.timeslots).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "if (res.timeslots && res.timeslots.length > 0) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('slotId', res.timeslots[0].slotId);",
                  "    console.log('slotId saved:', res.timeslots[0].slotId);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"startTime\": \"{{slotStart}}\",\n  \"endTime\": \"{{slotEnd}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mentors/{{mentorId}}/timeslots",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mentors", "{{mentorId}}", "timeslots"]
            },
            "description": "Create a time slot for the mentor. The pre-request script auto-fills tomorrow 10:00–11:00. Saves slotId."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
          "name": "Create Multiple Time Slots",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"slots\": [\n    { \"startTime\": \"{{slotStart}}\", \"endTime\": \"{{slotEnd}}\" },\n    { \"startTime\": \"2099-01-15T14:00:00.000Z\", \"endTime\": \"2099-01-15T15:00:00.000Z\" }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mentors/{{mentorId}}/timeslots",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mentors", "{{mentorId}}", "timeslots"]
            },
            "description": "Create several time slots in one request using the slots[] array."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000003-0000-0000-0000-000000000003",
          "name": "List Available Slots",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mentors/{{mentorId}}/timeslots",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mentors", "{{mentorId}}", "timeslots"]
            },
            "description": "List upcoming available time slots for the mentor."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Bookings",
      "item": [
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000004-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
          "name": "Create Booking",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test('booking in response', () => pm.expect(res.booking).to.be.an('object'));",
                  "if (res.booking) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('bookingId', res.booking.bookingId);",
                  "    console.log('bookingId saved:', res.booking.bookingId);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"mentorId\": \"{{mentorId}}\",\n  \"slotId\": \"{{slotId}}\",\n  \"studentId\": \"{{studentId}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/bookings",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["bookings"]
            },
            "description": "Book a session. Requires studentId, mentorId, and slotId to be set in collection variables. Saves bookingId."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000004-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
          "name": "Create Booking — double-book guard (expect 409)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('409 Conflict', () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"mentorId\": \"{{mentorId}}\",\n  \"slotId\": \"{{slotId}}\",\n  \"studentId\": \"{{studentId}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/bookings",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["bookings"]
            },
            "description": "Booking the same slot a second time must return 409 Conflict."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000004-0000-0000-0000-000000000003",
          "name": "List Mentor Bookings",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mentors/{{mentorId}}/bookings",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mentors", "{{mentorId}}", "bookings"]
            },
            "description": "All bookings for the mentor (upcoming + past)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000004-0000-0000-0000-000000000004",
          "name": "List Mentor Bookings — upcoming only",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mentors/{{mentorId}}/bookings?when=upcoming",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["mentors", "{{mentorId}}", "bookings"],
              "query": [{ "key": "when", "value": "upcoming" }]
            },
            "description": "Filter to only sessions in the future."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000004-0000-0000-0000-000000000005",
          "name": "Cancel Booking",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const res = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('cancelled flag', () => pm.expect(res.cancelled).to.be.true);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-student-id",
                "value": "{{studentId}}",
                "description": "Must match the student who created the booking"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{bookingId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Cancel a booking. x-student-id must match the booking owner — returns 403 otherwise."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "_postman_id": "11000004-0000-0000-0000-000000000006",
          "name": "Cancel Booking — wrong student (expect 403)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-student-id",
                "value": "wrong-student-id",
                "description": "Intentionally wrong — should return 403"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["bookings", "{{bookingId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Cancelling another student's booking must return 403 Forbidden."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
